Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `TradeReportID`: unique identifier of the trade → will be used as tradeID, filter / SELECT field  
• `MaturityDate`: contract‑expiry timestamp → used as tradeTimestamp  
• `TargetCompID`: first four characters map to the trading algorithm → used to derive algorithm  
• `Symbol`: the instrument’s ticker → symbol in the output  
• `LastPx`: price at which the CFD was entered → openPrice  
• `StrikePrice`: price at which the CFD closed → closePrice (used for sorting “highest closing prices”)  
• `Sides.Side`: LONG / SHORT flag that sits in the nested column `Sides` → tradeDirection  
• `Quantity`: overall quantity → can be inspected, optional condition (e.g. Quantity > 0)  
• `SendingTime`, `TransactTime`, `TradeDate`: may be useful for additional exploration but are not required for the final top‑6 list  

Typical conditions we might use  
• `WHERE StrikePrice IS NOT NULL` – ignore empty closing prices  
• `ORDER BY StrikePrice DESC` – rank by highest closing price  
• `QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER(ORDER BY StrikePrice DESC) <= 6` – keep the six largest values  

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Below are ten exploratory → increasingly complex BigQuery queries (each capped with LIMIT 20) that reveal useful values in the above columns and culminate in the final answer.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at the 20 largest closing prices in the whole table
SELECT StrikePrice
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`
WHERE StrikePrice IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY StrikePrice DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) List 20 distinct trading symbols
SELECT DISTINCT Symbol
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`
WHERE Symbol IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Show 20 different TargetCompID prefixes and the algorithm names they map to
SELECT DISTINCT
  SUBSTR(TargetCompID, 1, 4) AS prefix,
  CASE
    WHEN SUBSTR(TargetCompID, 1, 4) = 'MOMO' THEN 'Momentum'
    WHEN SUBSTR(TargetCompID, 1, 4) = 'LUCK' THEN 'Feeling Lucky'
    WHEN SUBSTR(TargetCompID, 1, 4) = 'PRED' THEN 'Prediction'
    ELSE 'Unknown'
  END AS algorithm
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Inspect side/direction values found inside the nested Sides column
SELECT DISTINCT s.Side
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`,
     UNNEST(Sides) AS s
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Pair StrikePrice with its trade direction to see whether LONG or SHORT trades differ in closing price
SELECT
  s.Side AS tradeDirection,
  t.StrikePrice AS closePrice
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report` AS t,
     UNNEST(t.Sides) AS s
WHERE t.StrikePrice IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY t.StrikePrice DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Display 20 trades with derived tradeMultiplier (1 for LONG, -1 for SHORT)
SELECT
  t.TradeReportID AS tradeID,
  s.Side AS tradeDirection,
  CASE WHEN s.Side = 'LONG' THEN 1 WHEN s.Side = 'SHORT' THEN -1 ELSE 0 END AS tradeMultiplier,
  t.StrikePrice AS closePrice
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report` AS t,
     UNNEST(t.Sides) AS s
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Show algorithm, symbol and closing price to check price dispersion by strategy
SELECT
  CASE
    WHEN SUBSTR(TargetCompID, 1, 4) = 'MOMO' THEN 'Momentum'
    WHEN SUBSTR(TargetCompID, 1, 4) = 'LUCK' THEN 'Feeling Lucky'
    WHEN SUBSTR(TargetCompID, 1, 4) = 'PRED' THEN 'Prediction'
    ELSE 'Unknown'
  END AS algorithm,
  Symbol,
  StrikePrice AS closePrice
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`
WHERE StrikePrice IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY closePrice DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) For the 20 most expensive trades, pull open vs. close prices
SELECT
  TradeReportID AS tradeID,
  LastPx        AS openPrice,
  StrikePrice   AS closePrice
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`
WHERE StrikePrice IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY closePrice DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Same as (8) but add tradeTimestamp and symbol for fuller context
SELECT
  TradeReportID        AS tradeID,
  MaturityDate         AS tradeTimestamp,
  Symbol,
  LastPx               AS openPrice,
  StrikePrice          AS closePrice
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report`
WHERE StrikePrice IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY closePrice DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) FINAL ANSWER – gather the requested fields for the top‑6 trades with the highest closing prices, including derived columns
SELECT
  t.TradeReportID                             AS tradeID,
  t.MaturityDate                              AS tradeTimestamp,
  CASE
    WHEN SUBSTR(t.TargetCompID, 1, 4) = 'MOMO' THEN 'Momentum'
    WHEN SUBSTR(t.TargetCompID, 1, 4) = 'LUCK' THEN 'Feeling Lucky'
    WHEN SUBSTR(t.TargetCompID, 1, 4) = 'PRED' THEN 'Prediction'
    ELSE 'Unknown'
  END                                          AS algorithm,
  t.Symbol                                    AS symbol,
  t.LastPx                                    AS openPrice,
  t.StrikePrice                               AS closePrice,
  s.Side                                      AS tradeDirection,
  CASE WHEN s.Side = 'SHORT' THEN -1
       WHEN s.Side = 'LONG'  THEN  1
       ELSE 0 END                             AS tradeMultiplier
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cymbal_investments.trade_capture_report` AS t
JOIN UNNEST(t.Sides) AS s
WHERE t.StrikePrice IS NOT NULL
QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY t.StrikePrice DESC) <= 6
LIMIT 20;
```

The tenth query returns the six trade reports with the highest `closePrice` (i.e., `StrikePrice`) together with every data field requested in the specification.
